invalid-define-component.js:6:5 lint/nursery/useVueComputedPropertyReturn ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The computed property foo doesn't always return a value.
  
    4 │ export default defineComponent({
    5 │   computed: {
  > 6 │     foo() {},
      │     ^^^^^^^^
    7 │   },
    8 │ });
  
  i Vue uses the value the getter returns as the value of the computed property. When the getter ends without a return statement, the computed property is undefined.
  
  i Make sure that every path through the getter ends with a return statement that returns a value.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

